From: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wave: preserve Linux netdev and bridge ownership

Bind AP_VLAN children to their parent and peer incarnation. Preserve ordinary
Linux bridge forwarding, hairpin, four-address teardown and accepted counters.
Keep proc readers and private netdev state alive through native retirement.

This is the final native integration against the pinned vendor source.
Firmware-dependent policy remains downstream with exact image admission.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>

